<para>For questions 4–7, recall the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">zero product property</term> means that each (or all) of the factors could be equal to zero when their product is zero. Solve each equation by setting each factor equal to zero and solving.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise><exercise>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-input-ack">
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x=0\) and \(x=\frac {-11}{2}\)</para>
  </div>
<problem>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x(2x+11)=0\)</item>
    </list>
  </problem><solution>
